  - path: docs/decisions/dec-32-curl-parser-accepts-what-a-browser-emits.html
    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "DEC-32, the why behind the parser's boundary. Context: copy-as-curl exists (UC-5), the inverse was requested at plan review, and curl has hundreds of flags behind a shell grammar, so the question was where to stop and what to do at the edge. Decision: accept what a developer actually pastes - a browser's Copy as cURL and toCurl - and refuse everything else naming the flag; a closed accepted set and a closed transfer-only set, a three-fates diagram (accepted/expanded, consumed, refused - no fourth), and the statement that the two lists are the arms of one lookup so code and record can only disagree if the code changes. Four alternatives rejected: reimplementing curl's CLI (hundreds of flags, most irrelevant to the wire, a permanent obligation), accepting everything and ignoring the unknown (-F ignored turns multipart into a bare POST, -G ignored moves the body - a flow subtly unlike the pasted request that the user cannot see), shelling out to curl (it would run the request, which is E-REPLAY, and tests could not be hermetic), and a shell-words dependency (the subset is small, refusals need their own wording, and $'...' which Chrome emits is outside what they read). The header-in-disguise rule as a table: a flag that IS a header expands because dropping it changes what the request is; curl's runtime defaults are never invented because the flow records the command not one tool's runtime (User-Agent: curl/8.x on a Chrome-copied request would be a lie) and because that is what keeps toCurl -> parse an exact inverse; headers in disguise a browser never emits (-A, -e, -r, -I) are refused and widening is a reopening of this record. The wire: raw body not JSON-wrapped (a wrapper adds a quoting layer to an input whose difficulty is quoting; the same bytes work from a shell with --data-binary @-), ?format=curl on the existing door with an unknown value refused naming format (the same rule ?source= follows), the refusal as HAR import's plain-text 400 written to be rendered verbatim on the paste target as the capture-controls design pinned before the parser existed, and the flow stamped at read time with HTTP/1.1 and no response. What the inverse guarantees and where it stops: equality on method, URI, headers and body proven as a property with the serializer mirrored and anchored to the TS pins, and the two shapes not round-tripped because curl itself drops or changes them (a blank header value written as -H 'Name: ', a GET with a body). Consequences: both sets closed with additions reopening the record; the Windows cmd shape refused not half-read; a pasted command is a second FORMAT behind the import door and the same mark, not a second capture format (DEC-30) and not a third provenance (DEC-31); the parser never runs the request (E-REPLAY). Ends with the one-fact-per-tier statement that the flag tables and grammar live only in src/api/curl.rs."
